# SRG-APP-000358-WSR-000063  -  CAT II
# The web server must not impede the ability to write specified log record
# content to an audit log server.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000358-WSR-000063
group:           V-206422
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001851
control_rev5:    AU-4

contribution:    The application's contribution is that its path to an audit log server is
                 configured and unobstructed: a target group names the receiving systems it
                 writes to.

governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.

check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/outputs.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The audit log server itself, its receiving port and its storage -
                 SPLK-CL-000150 places the matching inputs.conf on a separate instance
external:        The test the check text describes, in which a user generates events and
                 the data is observed arriving on the separate server, which is an operator
                 procedure rather than a configuration read
external:        Where a target group uses indexerDiscovery instead of a static server
                 list, the cluster manager that supplies the receivers

citation:        defaultGroup non_empty is removed for the reason given on
                 SRG-APP-000358-AU-000100: outputs.conf.spec:63-70 makes it optional,
                 overridable by _TCP_ROUTING, and "no longer required" since 4.2, so the
                 condition failed deployments that forward correctly through per-input
                 routing. The indexerDiscovery alternative to a static server list
                 (outputs.conf.spec:128) is recorded as an external dependency because the
                 vocabulary cannot express an either-or condition.
finding:         No forwarding target group names a receiving system, so the application
                 cannot write or transfer its log records to a separate audit log server.
